    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_36f12e00",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: who_farted_question_mark; hasOverallIntent: cyberbullying; overall-intent-description: The image features a Black man in formal attire with a serious, unamused facial expression, overlaid with the text 'who farted?'. This juxtaposition is a common internet meme format used to mock or ridicule someone for an embarrassing or socially awkward moment. The meme's intent is to create humor by implying the person is the source of an unpleasant event (farting), which is often used to belittle or embarrass the individual. While not explicitly violent or hateful, it targets the individual based on their race and appearance, fitting the category of cyberbullying as it uses visual and textual elements to disparage a specific person in a public context. The meme relies on the individual's recognizable features to generate the joke, which can be seen as a form of racial stereotyping or mockery, especially when paired with the absurdity of the question. The overall intent is to provoke laughter through humiliation, potentially at the expense of the person's dignity, and may contribute to a hostile or mocking online environment.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b1b996ce"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
